# 2.53.0

sched/fair: Restrict NI_RANDOM throttling to !SD_SHARE_LLC domains

On multi-LLC (multi-CCD) topologies, applying NI_RANDOM probabilistic
throttling across all scheduling domains starves intra-LLC cores of
work and allows sd->newidle_ratio to collapse toward zero during bursty
multi-threaded workloads.

Make three targeted adjustments to sched_balance_newidle():

 1. Abort the domain walk early if ttwu_pending or cfs.h_nr_queued
    becomes set while unlocked, avoiding remote pull collisions and
    unnecessary involuntary preemptions.

 2. Bypass NI_RANDOM inside SD_SHARE_LLC domains (SMT/MC) where scans
    are cheap and the L3 cache is shared.

 3. Clamp the minimum NI_RANDOM check weight to 32/1024 (~3.1%) on
    !SD_SHARE_LLC domains so cross-LLC bursts are rescued promptly
    while preserving decay via update_newidle_stats(sd, 0).

Benchmark on AMD Threadripper 9960X (24C/48T, 4 CCDs, NPS1, performance
governor @ 3.625 GHz min, teo cpuidle, libx264 1080p medium 42 threads):

 /usr/bin/time -v ffmpeg \
    -hide_banner -loglevel error \
    -i 2026-10-03_02-46-32.mkv \
    -map 0:v:0 \
    -vf "scale=1920:1080" \
    -c:v libx264 -preset medium -profile:v high \
    -b:v 8000k -maxrate 8000k -bufsize 8000k \
    -g 120 -keyint_min 120 -sc_threshold 0 \
    -x264-params aq-mode=2:me=umh:direct=auto:rc-lookahead=50:subme=8 \
    -threads 42 \
    -an -sn \
    -f null -

 Configuration          Elapsed    CPU %    User     System   Invol CS
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 Stock NI_RANDOM         19.70s    1913%   375.03s    1.91s    242,332
 Stock NO_NI_RANDOM      18.67s    2029%   374.63s    4.36s    840,725
 Patched (NI_RANDOM)     18.43s    2038%   373.63s    2.25s    508,080
 Patched + poc-smt -d    18.03s    2094%   376.24s    1.51s     81,044

 Patched NI_RANDOM outperforms stock NO_NI_RANDOM in wall-clock elapsed
 time (18.43s vs. 18.67s) while cutting system time by 48% (2.25s vs.
 4.36s) and involuntary context switches by 40% (508k vs. 840k).

