# 2.53.0

sched/fair: disable NI_RATE as default

The above patch handles intra-CCD balancing immediately (SD_SHARE_LLC) and
caps cross-CCD starvation via the 32/1024 floor. With that in place, NI_RATE
is no longer needed as a fallback mechanism and only adds scheduler noise on
multi-CCD topologies.

 Configuration          Elapsed    CPU %    User     System   Invol CS
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 Stock NI_RANDOM         19.70s    1913%   375.03s    1.91s    242,332
 Stock NO_NI_RANDOM      18.67s    2029%   374.63s    4.36s    840,725

 Patched (NI_RANDOM)     18.43s    2038%   373.63s    2.25s    508,080
 Plus NO_NI_RATE         18.37s    2055%   375.67s    1.89s    446,661

 Patched + poc-smt -d    18.03s    2094%   376.24s    1.51s     81,044
 Plus NO_NI_RATE         17.99s    2108%   378.00s    1.52s     82,174

Additionally, validated against the easyWave tsunami simulation benchmark
(which originally exposed the NI_RANDOM newidle_ratio collapse on LKML):

 OMP_NUM_THREADS=<N> ./src/easywave \
    -grid examples/e2Asean.grd -source examples/BengkuluSept2007.flt \
    -time 1200

 Configuration (Threadripper 9960X)         Threads   05:00:00    10:00:00
 -------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Pre-NI_RANDOM baseline (6.12.63 / 6.18.3)     48     2,908 ms         N/A
 Stock NI_RANDOM regression (6.12.66 / 6.18.6) 48    13,057 ms         N/A
 Patched NO_NI_RANDOM (7.4-rc2)                48     2,279 ms    9,827 ms
 Patched NI_RANDOM + NI_RATE (7.4-rc2)         48     3,227 ms   11,759 ms
 Patched NI_RANDOM + NO_NI_RATE (7.4-rc2)      48     4,796 ms   13,743 ms
 Patched NI_RANDOM + NO_NI_RATE (7.4-rc2)      24     1,924 ms    9,108 ms

While NI_RATE helps synthetic 100% SMT lockstep barriers (48 threads),
NO_NI_RATE achieves the fastest overall throughput at physical core count
(24 threads: 1,924 ms vs. 2,908 ms pre-regression) and outperforms across
real-world multi-threaded workloads (libaom, x265, libx264, Geekbench 6,
and partial-load desktop usage) without cross-CCD migration noise.

