# 2.53.0

sched/fair: Reduce newidle_ratio sample window to 512 (16/512 floor)

Halve the update_newidle_stats() sample window from 1024 to 512 calls
(adjusting the time-decay shift to delta >> 23) and set the minimum
!SD_SHARE_LLC check weight to 16/512 (exact 1/32 = 3.125% floor).

This cuts adaptation lag in half when workloads transition between idle
and active states while preserving the ~3.125% baseline cross-CCD rescue
rate—improving worst-case 48-thread OpenMP barrier latency, memory-bound
streaming throughput, and interactive GUI responsiveness without adding
involuntary context switch churn.

Benchmark comparison:
(1024 window @ 3.1% vs. 512 window @ 3.1%, NO_NI_RATE)

 Workload / Metric                    1024 Window    512 Window
 --------------------------------------------------------------
 easyWave 48T (05:00:00)                 4,796 ms      3,467 ms
 easyWave 48T (10:00:00)                13,743 ms     11,898 ms
 easyWave 24T (05:00:00)                 1,924 ms      1,908 ms
 easyWave 24T (10:00:00)                 9,108 ms      9,228 ms
 ffmpeg 42T smt=1 (Elapsed)                18.37s        18.41s
 ffmpeg 42T smt=1 (Invol CS)              446,661       446,887
 ffmpeg 42T poc-smt -d (Elapsed)           17.99s        17.92s
 ffmpeg 42T poc-smt -d (Invol CS)          82,174        80,906

